 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Existence of an ideal defining the complement of a qc open",
 "statement": "Let $W\\subseteq Y$ be a quasi-compact open in a qcqs scheme. There exists\na finite type quasi-coherent ideal $\\mathcal I\\subseteq\\mathcal O_Y$ such\nthat $V(\\mathcal I)=Y\\setminus W$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-blowups/lemma-nagata-qc-open-complement-ideal-exists.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-qc-open-complement-ideal-exists, order 168"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-extended-ideal"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Let $\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\mathcal O_Y$ be the quasi-coherent ideal defining\nthe reduced induced closed subscheme on $Y\\setminus W$. Its restriction to\n$W$ is the unit ideal. Apply the general submodule form of\n[lemma-nagata-finite-type-ideal-extension-exists] with ambient module\n$\\mathcal K$ and submodule $\\mathcal O_W=\\mathcal K|_W$. It gives a finite\ntype quasi-coherent submodule $\\mathcal I\\subseteq\\mathcal K$ with\n$\\mathcal I|_W=\\mathcal O_W$. As an $\\mathcal O_Y$-submodule of the ideal\n$\\mathcal K$, the sheaf $\\mathcal I$ is itself an ideal.\nThe inclusion $\\mathcal I\\subseteq\\mathcal K$ gives\n$Y\\setminus W=V(\\mathcal K)\\subseteq V(\\mathcal I)$, while\n$\\mathcal I|_W=\\mathcal O_W$ gives the reverse containment. Hence\n$V(\\mathcal I)=Y\\setminus W$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-finite-type-ideal-extension-exists"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
